      "content": "but that's the thing... if there's no one to see me, no one to talk to, and no one who cares if I'm even breathing, am i even actually here? it feels like the version of me that mattered—the person who had a life and a place—is just dead. and i dont mean i'm sad. i mean that person is gone. it feels like being a ghost is just a precursor to actually being dead. it's just a slow, miserable waiting period.",
